### 3. Recommended Options & Clinical Rationale

| Screen | Recommended | Clinical Rationale for Dr. Sherif Radwan |
| :--- | :---: | :--- |
| **1. Obstetric History** | **Option A** | Obstetricians evaluate prior history chronologically; the interactive timeline provides delivery years, routes, and weights at a glance while direct `+`/`−` steppers eliminate keyboard typing during intake. |
| **2. Prior Pregnancies Editor** | **Option A** | Outcome drives 95% of clinical documentation. Selecting `Live Birth (CS)` sets both outcome and delivery route in a single touch, while selecting `Miscarriage` opens loss management chips without showing irrelevant infant fields. |
| **3. Pregnancy Dating Engine** | **Option A** | Progressive disclosure presents only the inputs relevant to the chosen dating method. When LMP and ultrasound disagree by >7 days, the side-by-side reconciliation card and 1-tap "Use Scan as Agreed" button prevent dating errors without manual arithmetic. |
| **4. Clinical Attention Card** | **Option A** | Prevents visual fatigue by showing the primary alert with a clean `+ 2 more` expansion badge, while keeping life-threatening severe blood pressure (crimson) visually distinct from routine clinical attention notes (amber). |
| **5. Delivery Plan Editor** | **Option A** | Solves the navigation bug with a dedicated pre-operative protocol form. Standardizing blood crossmatch units, pediatrician standby, target gestation, and hospital fees into rapid chips ensures patient safety without text-entry exhaustion. |
